  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "An organic compound undergoes first-order decomposition. The time taken for its decomposition to $1 /$ 8 and $1 / 10$ of its initial concentration are $t_{1 / 8}$ and $t_{1 / 10}$ respectively. What is the value of $\\left[\\frac{t_{1 / 8}}{t_{1 / 10}}\\right] \\times 10$ ? $\\left(\\log _{10} 2=0.3\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n t_{1 / 8}=\\frac{2.303 \\log 8}{k}=\\frac{2.303 \\times 3 \\log 2}{k} \\\\\r\n\r\nt_{1 / 10}=\\frac{2.303}{k} \\log 10=\\frac{2.303}{k} \\\\\r\n\r\n{\\left[\\frac{t_{1 / 8}}{t_{1 / 10}}\\right] \\times 10=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2.303 \\times 3 \\log 2}{k}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{2.303}{k}\\right)} \\times 10=9}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
